{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bil9iq7sx","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MtTHvBvD2dqg5DdknkNeyY","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/a3940a29-0418-4168-8306-ddbf2cf5e587/tasks/bil9iq7sx.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_0\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nPeople judge randomness by the variety of short patterns a sequence contains: reading it as overlapping chunks of one to four flips, a sequence looks random to the extent that its chunks are all different from one another (many distinct chunks for its length), and repetitive to the extent that the same few chunks recur — whether through a long streak, strict alternation, or an almost-repeating unit with one slip. People differ in how strongly this felt variety drives their choice. This disagrees most sharply with the switch-rate-ideal incumbent on pairs with similar switch counts where one sequence reuses its chunks (near-periodic sequences such as HTTHTTHH, or ones with a long streak) and on block-structured sequences like HHTTHHTT, whose middling switch rate the incumbent rates as plausible but whose chunk variety is low.\nEOF\necho chunk_variety_subword_complexity > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/candidate.py\n\"\"\"Chunk variety (subword complexity) judgement of randomness.\n\nPeople judge randomness by the variety of short patterns a sequence contains:\nread as overlapping chunks of one to four flips, a sequence looks random to the\nextent that its chunks are all different (many distinct chunks for its length)\nand repetitive to the extent that the same few chunks recur — a long streak,\nstrict alternation, or an almost-repeating unit. People differ in how strongly\nthis felt variety drives their choice.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pymc as pm\n\nMAX_CHUNK = 4\n\n\ndef compute_features(sequence_a, sequence_b):\n    def variety(seq):\n        n = len(seq)\n        scores = []\n        for k in range(1, min(MAX_CHUNK, n) + 1):\n            chunks = {seq[i:i + k] for i in range(n - k + 1)}\n            possible = min(2 ** k, n - k + 1)\n            scores.append(len(chunks) / possible)\n        return float(np.mean(scores))\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()\n    b = sequence_b.strip().upper()\n    return {\"variety_a\": variety(a), \"variety_b\": variety(b)}\n\n\nN_SLOTS = 400\n\nwith pm.Model() as model:\n    var_a = pm.Data(\"variety_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    var_b = pm.Data(\"variety_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n\n    # Person-specific sensitivity to chunk variety (log-normal population).\n    mu_log_beta = pm.Normal(\"mu_log_beta\", mu=1.5, sigma=1.5)\n    sigma_log_beta = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_log_beta\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_beta = pm.Normal(\"z_beta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=N_SLOTS)\n    beta = pm.Deterministic(\"beta\", pm.math.exp(mu_log_beta + sigma_log_beta * z_beta))\n\n    score = beta[participant_id] * (var_a - var_b)\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(score))\n\n    chose_left = pm.Data(\"chose_left\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n    pm.Bernoulli(\"response\", p=p_left, observed=chose_left)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses $D/../../responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"6391cbf0-0f64-4673-bb4a-0477294ab653","session_id":"a3940a29-0418-4168-8306-ddbf2cf5e587"}
